<Folder><name>Eat</name>
<Placemark><name>Sushi Rairaku</name><description>Sushi &amp; Seafood
鮨 らい落
New Ginza sushi counter, a branch of the hard-to-book Sushi Murayama. The chef trained at Sushi Taichi. Full omakase for ¥25,000 (most Ginza omakase start at ¥30,000–40,000). Fish comes straight from Toyosu, with red-vinegar rice. Book early.
https://www.threads.com/@mark25tw88/post/DfI1lfwn9tU
(approximate location)</description><Point><coordinates>139.765,35.6717,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Ginza Sushi-dokoro Maguro Soma Suisan</name><description>Sushi &amp; Seafood
銀座寿司処 まぐろ相馬水産
Good-quality Ginza sushi. The chef is the highlight: funny and warm even if you don&#x27;t speak Japanese.
https://www.threads.com/@jackbb988/post/DfQ65cxCZNb
(approximate location)</description><Point><coordinates>139.765,35.6717,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Nakamata (tuna &amp; seafood rice bowls)</name><description>Sushi &amp; Seafood
まぐろと魚 海鮮めし なかまた
Behind Kabukiza. Uses tuna from Toyosu wholesaler Yamayuki. Bowls from ¥1,980; the top &quot;everything&quot; bowl is ¥6,480. Eat it three ways: wasabi soy, then sesame + sweet soy, then egg yolk. Open 11:00–21:00. Exit A6 of Ginza Stn (5 min) or exit 3 of Higashi-Ginza (1 min).
https://www.instagram.com/reel/Deo9tDpiovI/</description><Point><coordinates>139.76886,35.67033,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Yoroniku Tokyo (Azabudai Hills)</name><description>Wagyu, Yakiniku &amp; Sukiyaki
YORONIKU TOKYO 麻布台ヒルズ
&quot;Possibly the best yakiniku of my life.&quot; Premium yakiniku on Tower Plaza 3F, Azabudai Hills.
https://www.instagram.com/reel/DeJkbpwx87j/</description><Point><coordinates>139.740921,35.661549,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Ushigoro S. Shinjuku</name><description>Wagyu, Yakiniku &amp; Sukiyaki
USHIGORO S. 新宿
A5 Kuroge wagyu grilled for you by staff, with private rooms. Must-try: the wagyu sando with fresh black truffle and the thick-cut tongue. On 11F.
https://www.instagram.com/reel/DeyzGNpP19n/</description><Point><coordinates>139.702774,35.692207,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Ginza Chikamitsu</name><description>Wagyu, Yakiniku &amp; Sukiyaki
銀座 ちかみつ
Tabelog Top 100 (2025). Famous for its &quot;uni wagyu hot dog&quot;: wagyu tartare topped with two kinds of sea urchin.
https://www.instagram.com/reel/DeyzGNpP19n/</description><Point><coordinates>139.764664,35.668221,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Kumasan Azabu</name><description>Wagyu, Yakiniku &amp; Sukiyaki
くま3 麻布
Creative wagyu kaiseki with very pretty dishes (bear-shaped monaka, mini burgers). Great for photos, though the reviewer found the taste less memorable.
https://www.instagram.com/reel/DeyzGNpP19n/
(approximate location)</description><Point><coordinates>139.7365,35.6565,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Yakiniku A-bull Ikebukuro (&quot;ex-boyfriend set&quot;)</name><description>Wagyu, Yakiniku &amp; Sukiyaki
焼肉 A-bull 池袋
Near Don Quijote Ikebukuro. Ask staff for the off-menu &quot;前男友套餐&quot; (ex-boyfriend set). Very good value and filling.
https://www.threads.com/@stay.with.yue/post/DfORvyGE6YE
(approximate location)</description><Point><coordinates>139.714,35.731,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Miraku-tei (old-town yakiniku since 1975)</name><description>Wagyu, Yakiniku &amp; Sukiyaki
味樂亭 荒川区
Family-run yakiniku in Arakawa-ku, open since 1975, with a Showa-era, local feel. Order the beef tongue (タン), skirt (ハラミ) and premium loin (上ロース). Cheaper than the famous central shops.
https://www.threads.com/@fattsai/post/DfRr9qyCbdO
(approximate location)</description><Point><coordinates>139.783,35.736,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Shabuzen Shibuya (all-you-can-eat wagyu sukiyaki)</name><description>Wagyu, Yakiniku &amp; Sukiyaki
しゃぶ禅 渋谷店
Open 40 years. All-you-can-eat Kuroge wagyu sukiyaki for ¥9,000 / 120 min, with very attentive refills. Open 17:00–23:00. In B1 of Shibuya Creston Hotel.
https://www.instagram.com/reel/DdZAv4uIpRF/</description><Point><coordinates>139.694946,35.66317,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>One-person A5 wagyu sukiyaki under ¥1,500 (Nihonbashi)</name><description>Wagyu, Yakiniku &amp; Sukiyaki
日本橋（店名: 一り?）
A5 wagyu, one pot per person, under ¥1,500. In a reply the author gave the shop name as roughly &quot;Nihonbashi 1ri&quot; (日本橋 一り?). Long queue, so go early. The name is uncertain; check the link.
https://www.threads.com/@travelfish.jp/post/DfJ-BE6jyiG
(approximate location)</description><Point><coordinates>139.7745,35.684,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Dote no Iseya (tempura since 1889)</name><description>Tonkatsu, Tempura &amp; Japanese
土手の伊勢屋
One of Tokyo&#x27;s oldest tempura-bowl shops (1889), in a historic building. Expect queues of up to ~2 hours.
https://www.threads.com/@tequila187110/post/DfQeLZNFeDQ</description><Point><coordinates>139.797012,35.725098,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tempura Motoyoshi (2 Michelin stars)</name><description>Tonkatsu, Tempura &amp; Japanese
天ぷら 元吉
The original shop behind Taipei/Hsinchu &quot;Motoichi&quot; tempura. Big portions; matsutake tempura in season. The reviewer booked through the Palace Hotel concierge and felt the Taipei branch was just as good.
https://www.threads.com/@easyrush/post/DfRYudEGSwY
(approximate location)</description><Point><coordinates>139.717,35.6705,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Toritsune Shizendo (oyakodon)</name><description>Tonkatsu, Tempura &amp; Japanese
鳥つね 自然洞
Rated 4.3. Superb oyakodon (chicken &amp; egg rice bowl). Near Suehirocho / Yushima.
https://www.instagram.com/p/DebzBHhCdJ5/</description><Point><coordinates>139.771301,35.704308,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tofu Cuisine Sorano Shibuya</name><description>Tonkatsu, Tempura &amp; Japanese
豆腐料理 空野 渋谷店
A break from sushi and ramen: tofu-focused set meals in Sakuragaoka (Cherry Garden 1F).
https://www.instagram.com/p/De18xTDJmef/</description><Point><coordinates>139.70369,35.654591,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>EDW yellow Shibuya (omurice)</name><description>Tonkatsu, Tempura &amp; Japanese
EDW yellow Shibuya
Recommended twice in the list. &quot;Best omurice I&#x27;ve had.&quot; Add the butter crab croquette; the ice-cream French toast is a must.
https://www.instagram.com/reel/DfMgbxkyxtg/
(approximate location)</description><Point><coordinates>139.698,35.6605,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Rikyu Gyutan Shinjuku</name><description>Tonkatsu, Tempura &amp; Japanese
利久 牛たん 新宿
Sendai-style grilled beef tongue with grated yam and oxtail soup: &quot;the perfect combo&quot;.
https://www.instagram.com/reel/DfMgbxkyxtg/
(approximate location)</description><Point><coordinates>139.702,35.692,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Shinjuku oden restaurant (Nagoya-style)</name><description>Tonkatsu, Tempura &amp; Japanese
新宿 関東煮
&quot;The best oden I have ever had.&quot; No queue and mostly Japanese customers; the desserts are great too. A commenter says it is a Nagoya chain. The name is only in the photo.
https://www.threads.com/@yy_o512/post/DfMazm4krdj
(approximate location)</description><Point><coordinates>139.7,35.691,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Godaime Hanayama Udon Ginza</name><description>Ramen, Udon &amp; Noodles
五代目 花山うどん 銀座店
Famous for &quot;Oni-himokawa&quot; extra-wide udon. Extremely popular: the author arrived at 10:50, before opening, and noodles were already sold out. Go very early.
https://www.threads.com/@will901215/post/DfLrDMuEu18</description><Point><coordinates>139.769073,35.669971,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Junteuchi Men to Mirai (Shimokitazawa)</name><description>Ramen, Udon &amp; Noodles
純手打ち 麺と未来
Michelin-recommended, Tabelog 3.77. Hand-made noodles wider than udon, big shrimp wontons, and a ¥300 seared chashu rice bowl. Weekdays 11:30–14:30, 17:30–21:00; weekends/holidays 11:30–17:00 or until sold out.
https://www.threads.com/@jaybinjapan/post/DfPeX1VkXsM</description><Point><coordinates>139.668671,35.663475,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>400°C Pizza Tokyo (Kagurazaka)</name><description>Ramen, Udon &amp; Noodles
400℃ Pizza Tokyo
Tabelog Top 100 pizza near Iidabashi / Kagurazaka. Favourites: FNT, Neve (all-white) and prosciutto. Casual, made for sharing.
https://www.threads.com/@easyrush/post/DfMQJ1TmVL_
(approximate location)</description><Point><coordinates>139.7405,35.7015,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>BONGEN COFFEE Tokyo Nihonbashi</name><description>Cafes &amp; Coffee
BONGEN COFFEE 日本橋
Famous &quot;life-changing iced latte&quot;. Choose your shot strength (regular / BONGEN / RICH) and one of four roasts. Iced BONGEN latte (dark) ¥990. Bigger than the main store; arrive soon after opening at 10am. Near Nihonbashi / Takaracho / Kyobashi stations.
https://www.threads.com/@orlando071233/post/DfWnjHJFLzI
(approximate location)</description><Point><coordinates>139.7765,35.6795,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Glitch Coffee &amp; Roasters</name><description>Cafes &amp; Coffee
GLITCH COFFEE &amp; ROASTERS
Light-roast specialty coffee in Jimbocho. Its beans are a classic Tokyo coffee souvenir.
https://www.threads.com/@maikeduo.roasters/post/DfLzxk2k9rP</description><Point><coordinates>139.761383,35.693691,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Hachijuhachi Ryoyosha (matcha, Asakusa)</name><description>Cafes &amp; Coffee
八十八良葉舎 浅草
Matcha drinks; add a scoop of ice cream. Also on the 15-place list below.
https://www.threads.com/@om__way/post/DfLtAV6GI6A
(approximate location)</description><Point><coordinates>139.7955,35.7115,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Starbucks Nippori</name><description>Cafes &amp; Coffee
スターバックス 日暮里
Beautifully designed, spacious Starbucks with an art exhibition (you can buy the artwork). 2 drinks + 2 food ≈ ¥2,264.
https://www.threads.com/@jackbb988/post/DfPYTxwCamS
(approximate location)</description><Point><coordinates>139.771,35.728,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Latte Art Mania Ginza (pudding &amp; latte art)</name><description>Cafes &amp; Coffee
LATTE ART MANIA GINZA
Calm Ginza café for custard pudding and latte art.
https://www.threads.com/@latteartmania_ginza/post/DfVt1OHFV43
(approximate location)</description><Point><coordinates>139.764,35.67,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tas Yard (French toast)</name><description>Sweets &amp; Bakery
Tas Yard タスヤード
&quot;Godly French toast.&quot; Weekdays 11:30–18:00, weekends 11:30–19:00. Google 4.1. Tel +81 3-3470-3940.
https://www.instagram.com/reel/Db2km16yfOI/</description><Point><coordinates>139.705872,35.675556,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>HAL&#x27;S BAGEL Jiyugaoka</name><description>Sweets &amp; Bakery
HAL&#x27;S BAGEL. 自由が丘店
A &quot;bagel theme park&quot; with 33 chewy bagels baked daily, plus Christmas flavours (raspberry cocoa, snow mocha). Red velvet ¥580, caramel brûlée ¥530. Open 10:00–18:00; expect a queue.
https://www.instagram.com/p/DfRvjdhjUNM/</description><Point><coordinates>139.669586,35.607334,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>L&#x27;Atelier du Pain Roppongi</name><description>Sweets &amp; Bakery
L&#x27;Atelier du Pain 六本木
Tabelog Top 100 bakery. Get the No.1 Roppongi salt bread (moist and springy) and the croissants. Country loaf on weekends only.
https://www.threads.com/@kkoinjp/post/DfOZ9tYIymq
(approximate location)</description><Point><coordinates>139.7315,35.6635,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>noix de beurre (Ginza Mitsukoshi B2)</name><description>Sweets &amp; Bakery
ノワ・ドゥ・ブール 銀座三越
Financiers fresh from the oven (crisp outside, soft inside), plus choux, Mont Blanc and strawberry tarts. Good gift boxes. From a Tokyo dessert round-up post.
https://www.threads.com/@ruanmianmian559/post/DfRDQ3OEug7</description><Point><coordinates>139.765594,35.671577,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Pudding tart at Tokyo Station</name><description>Sweets &amp; Bakery
東京駅 プリンタルト
&quot;Life-changing&quot; pudding tart sold only in Tokyo, inside Tokyo Station. Baked twice a day: weekdays 9:30 &amp; 17:00, weekends/holidays 9:00 &amp; 17:00. The shop name is only in the photo.
https://www.threads.com/@zhulaicai688/post/DfOC7LAn7Au
(approximate location)</description><Point><coordinates>139.7671,35.6812,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Medel deli, Ebisu (acai &amp; yogurt bowls)</name><description>Sweets &amp; Bakery
medel deli 恵比寿
Acai and yogurt bowls with generous toppings, plus light burgers and shakes. From a list of 5 favourite spots in Ebisu.
https://www.instagram.com/reel/DfLx7nju5RZ/
(approximate location)</description><Point><coordinates>139.7095,35.6475,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tofu Shokudo, Ebisu</name><description>Tonkatsu, Tempura &amp; Japanese
豆富食堂 恵比寿
Popular tofu set meals: a big slab of simmered tofu in light dashi, with soy-milk dessert.
https://www.instagram.com/reel/DfLx7nju5RZ/
(approximate location)</description><Point><coordinates>139.711,35.6462,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Arai Buhei Shoten: golden miso dango (Kawagoe)</name><description>Sweets &amp; Bakery
新井武平商店 川越時の鐘店
Huge chewy dango brushed with century-old Chichibu miso and grilled over charcoal. ¥500. Near the Toki no Kane bell tower.
https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZSUFTDNCyo/</description><Point><coordinates>139.48262,35.92355,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
