<Placemark><name>Kawagoe (&quot;Little Edo&quot;) day trip</name><description>Day Trips
川越
Preserved Edo-era warehouse streets, about 30 min from central Tokyo. Fastest: Ikebukuro → Kawagoe by Kawagoe Limited Express (25–30 min), or Seibu-Shinjuku → Hon-Kawagoe by Koedo limited express (~45 min). Lots of street food.
https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZSUFTDNCyo/</description><Point><coordinates>139.4858,35.9251,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Naritasan Omotesando &amp; Shinshoji (last-day trip)</name><description>Day Trips
成田山表参道・新勝寺
Under 10 min from Narita Airport. Edo-style street with grilled eel, the 1,000-year-old Shinshoji temple, and matcha sweets at old teahouses. Good for an afternoon or evening flight.
https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbvK3SDvvtf/</description><Point><coordinates>140.318,35.7856,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
