<Folder><name>Transport</name>
<Placemark><name>NRT-TYO Bus (Narita ⇄ Tokyo Station, ¥1,500)</name><description>Airport Transfer
東京シャトル / NRT-TYO BUS
About 1 hour, every ~10 min in the daytime, with Wi-Fi and staff help with luggage. ¥1,500 (child ¥750); ¥3,000 for 23:00–4:59 departures. Tickets: Narita T1/T2/T3 arrivals LCB counter; in Tokyo, at the Yaesu South Exit JR highway bus ticket office.
https://www.instagram.com/p/Dc5-1GYzKWV/</description><Point><coordinates>139.7695,35.679,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Skyliner face-recognition ticket gates</name><description>Airport Transfer
スカイライナー 顔認証
Buy and pay on the Skyliner website before your trip and register your face; then walk through the gates with no queue. Works at Narita T1, T2/3, Keisei Ueno and Nippori.
https://www.instagram.com/p/DaVHfyaBMr8/</description><Point><coordinates>139.774,35.7114,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Shinjuku Station survival guide</name><description>Getting Around
新宿駅 攻略
Lost? Find JR signs first. East = 3D cat (Kabukicho, Isetan). West = Metropolitan Govt Building (free night view, Omoide Yokocho, Yodobashi). South / New South = NEWoMan, Suica Penguin square, Busta bus terminal on 4F. Southeast = BEAMS, Shinjuku Gyoen.
https://www.instagram.com/p/Dd-ynzizrnY/</description><Point><coordinates>139.7006,35.6896,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Info &amp; Tips</name>
<Placemark><name>Narita T2 refund: real experience</name><description>Tax Refund (new system from 2026-11-01)
成田二航退稅心得
After entering departures, turn left to the row of refund kiosks at the end. With a card pre-linked online, just scan your passport: green = done, red = see customs. For cash, find &quot;Self Tax Refund&quot; between check-in counters A–C. Very fast.
https://www.threads.com/@vibeboyvibe/post/DfL7tumoznD</description><Point><coordinates>140.3929,35.772,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
